    "created_at": "2020-08-06T16:26:13Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-08-06T16:27:44Z",
    "body": "> I think it would be more helpful to start earlier in the process of https://whatwg.org/faq#adding-new-features. The linked document seems to be some sort of API documentation (I'm not sure for what... a mix of the select element as it exists today, and some future proposal?).\r\n\r\nAs noted in this [issue comment regarding meta](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/5793#issuecomment-670029539) Yes this is a future proposal and I'd prefer to avoid producing yet another document that is outlined in this [explainer](https://github.com/MicrosoftEdge/MSEdgeExplainers/blob/main/ControlUICustomization/explainer.md) unless absolutely necessary which is what is driving the Open UI effort which identifies these gaps.\r\n\r\n> I'm not sure for what... a mix of the select element as it exists today, and some future proposal?\r\n\r\nYeah, this is the output from Open UI as everyone building a component/control ends up building a specification like this. There is currently no one place to get all ARIA, HTML, CSS, etc in one place. So Open UI aims to fix this and hopefully simplify implementation efforts for anyone building a control/component (we've found even native control teams (UA and OS) do this same work up until the specific web platform [eg: ARIA adjustments]). I can do the FAQ but am curious if I should do a holistic FAQ for `<select>` in general and outline the currently known gaps identified in Open UI rather than *just* for `open` state.",
