    "created_at": "2020-08-06T16:32:52Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-08-06T16:32:52Z",
    "body": "To give an idea of why the linked explainer is not very helpful for this issue, its goals section does not list anything about an \"open\" state. Ctrl+Fing for \"open\" has a lot of false positives, but the only related sentence I can find is\r\n\r\n> Additional states for the controls will also be standardized as appropriate, such as an open state for `<select>` to allow styling like the following:\r\n\r\nwhich doesn't really explain _why_ someone would want to style the open state, or discuss why it would need a HTML proposal (as opposed to a CSS proposal).",
